{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0) or shows strong bearish signals.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes by applying a 10-15% dampening factor to the immediate next period.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is consistently above true outcome over 5+ days, gradually reduce forecast by 1-2% per day until convergence.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent true outcomes when sentiment is neutral or mildly bullish (sentiment ≈ 0), especially in the 3-5 day horizon.",
    "When sentiment shows a clear upward trend (e.g., >0.33 over 3+ consecutive days), slightly increase forecast lag by 1-2 days to avoid overreaction.",
    "For long-term (10+ day) forecasts, apply a smoothing filter to reduce volatility and avoid overfitting to recent spikes."
  ]
}
